Abstract = {People living now in urban area in most of isolated territory and tend
   to separated each other from a socio-cultural standpoint which is not
   found in Kotagede, Yogyakarta. Shared spaces and public accesses that
   passing private properties are naturally exsist. Many of spaces,
   artifacts and people life were relatively remains the same for several
   decades. A study that based on the paradigm of
   architectural-anthropology is intended to explore the ability of
   inhabitant to face the compulsion of cultural urbanization. The results
