   Kota Kinabalu, MALAYSIA, JAN 04-05, 2014},
Organization = {CE Bs; FAPS; UiTM},
Abstract = {This research investigated the relation between conscientiousness,
   collectivism, and corrupt tendency-which is represented by moral
   emotions ( shame and guilt proneness). The study was conducted on 117
   students ( 76 male, 41 female; M = 18.93 years old; SD = 1.67 years old)
   in Jakarta. The result shows that collectivism has positive predictive
   correlation with the tendency of not doing corruption and that
   conscientiousness is not able to predict corrupt tendencies.
   Collectivism of which every group member has as a strong moral identity
   is suggested to be the ideal ecological situation which need to be built
   to prevent corruption in Indonesia. (C) 2014 The Authors. Published by
   Elsevier Ltd.},
