   AND DEVELOPMENT},
Year = {2010},
Pages = {423-429},
Note = {2010 International Conference on Environmental Science and Development,
   Singapore, SINGAPORE, FEB 26-28, 2010},
Organization = {IACSIT; Environm Sci Soc},
Abstract = {Haidian District is a key ecological zone in Beijing. Forestry
   eco-compensation policies have been implemented in Haidian for five
   years. This paper investigated the eco-compensation practice in Haidian
   through interpreting policies, interviewing relevant personnel,
   questionnaires and statistic analysis. It examined the effectiveness and
   efficiency of implementing eco-compensation policies from both aspect of
   forestry eco-environment quality and aspect of the aspect of social
   economical benefit. The author analyzed the completeness of current
   forestry eco-compensation policies, the rationality and
   scientific-efficiency of the policies, the approach of compensation and
   the results of compensation. Based on the analysis, the author
   specifically proposed on how to improve forestry eco-compensation
   policies, how to form scientific compensation standards, how to enrich
   forest management models, and how to enhance self-compensation ability
   in agriculture and forestry.},
