   Sustainability and Quality of Life, Boston, MA, JUN 20-23, 2010},
Abstract = {Field monitoring was conducted in Bangkok to investigate the situation
   of traffic emission exposure of roadside pedestrians. From a viewpoint
   of actual exposure of pedestrians, short-term variations of air
   pollutant levels are significant, however, such data have been limited
   until recently. Hence, time-series data of traffic flows, polycyclic
   aromatic hydrocarbons monitored by real-time photoelectric aerosol
   sensors and vehicle exhaust detected as uncomfortable odor to
   pedestrians were obtained at very fine time resolution and their
   short-term peak patterns were analyzed by spectral analysis.
   Furthermore, conditions of the peak exposure occurrences and
   interrelations of those temporal variations were discussed (C) 2009
