Note = {7th International Conference Early Childhood Care and Education (ECCE),
   Moscow, RUSSIA, MAY 17-20, 2018},
Abstract = {Children's attitude to physical training lessons largely depends on that
   what motivates them to act. Motives, i.e. motivators, form under the
   influence of the child's living conditions and determine the orientation
   of his activity. The study has examined the motives of physical activity
   (educational, gaming, motive of health, strength, beauty, motive-praise,
   and motive under compulsion). An essential condition for motivating
   physical activity is the positive emotional background of physical
   activity, which is largely provided by an appropriate exercise load and
   availability of exercises offered to children. In its turn, children's
   emotional state is greatly influenced by the attitude of a teacher to
   physical exercises and the form of his communication with children. The
   teacher should understand the main motives of the child's behaviour and
   the ways of implementing them, he should know how these motives and ways
   correspond to the social and moral standards of his life and activity,
   and comprehend a wide variety of children's emotional experiences
   arising in each specific situation. Only taking into account these
   peculiarities, the teacher can cope with the tasks of physical education
   that he faces. This research is devoted to the study of motives and
   emotions of preschool children and primary school pupils. (C) 2018
   Published by Future Academy www.FutureAcademy.org.UK},
