Abstract = {Public Transport (PT) is supposed to be probably the most up-to-date
   answer to the growing need for relieving traffic congestion, the
   associated environmental problems and the continuously increasing cost
   for transferring passengers. The expansion of urban centres cannot
   support a PT system that would serve the passenger directly from the
   origin to the destination point. The combination of various modes of
   transport between trip ends represents the new reality. The aim of this
   paper is to present general guidelines for securing safe and comfortable
   transfers between different transport modes.},
