   HELSINKI, FINLAND, AUG 26-30, 1996},
Organization = {Int Assoc Meteorol \& Atmospher Sci; Int Commiss Clouds \& Precipitat;
   Comm Nucleat \& Atmospher Aerosols; Int Global Atmospher Chem Project;
   Univ Helsinki, Dept Phys; Finnish Meteorol Inst; Finnish Assoc Aerosol
   Res; Univ Helsinki, Lahti Res \& Training Ctr; Minist Educ Finland; Acad
   Finland; Finnair; Maj \& Tor Nessling Fdn; Neste Fdn},
Abstract = {Polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon (PAH) samples in the ambient air of
   rural, urban and traffic-intersection site have been collected by PS-1
   samplers, NRI (Noll Rotary Impactor) and MOUDIs (Micro-orifice Uniform
   Deposit Impacters) from July, 1993 to January, 1995 in southern Taiwan.
   Total-PAH concentrations averaged 496, 1300 and 4090 ng/m(3) for rural,
   urban and traffic intersection on the 1.5 m level, respectively. Mean
   gas phase distribution of total-PAHs was 72.4\%, 84.2\%, and 77.3\% for
   the rural, urban, and traffic intersection on the 1.5m level,
   respectively. Particle-bound total PAHs averaged 1930, 1840 and 1020 mu
   g/g for rural, urban and traffic intersection on the 1.5m level,
   respectively. For the traffic intersection, the particle size
   distribution (dC/dlogDp vs. Dp) of total-PAHs was found to have bimodal
   size distribution and are dominant in the fine particle mode (Dp < 1.0
   mu m).},
