Note = {24th International Symposium on Research and Applications in Psychology
   (SICAP) - Cognitive Characteristics of Transdisciplinarity. Applications
   in Psychology and Psychotherapies, Timisoara, ROMANIA, MAR 24-26, 2017},
Abstract = {This study aims to investigate the impact of the type of attachment and
   of the parental educational style existing in families of origin, on
   adolescents as well as to highlight different developed coping
   strategies. The data were collected by using three types of
   questionnaires applied on a sample of 79 adolescents. The attachment
   pattern and the coping strategy; the educational style used by parents
   and coping strategies are studies. The findings of the study suggest the
   importance of the attachment pattern and of the type of education
   manifested in the relationship between parent and adolescents and reveal
   the way in which some adolescents use certain coping strategies as a
   means of adaptation to the stressful events occurring in their life.},
