   Regeneration, Chung Ang Univ, Dept Urban Design \& Studies, Seoul, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-27, 2014},
Organization = {Assoc Malaysian Environm Behav Researchers},
Abstract = {In Malaysia, scant research has been conducted in understanding how
   students perceived the performance of service quality of student
   housing; and how they translated their perceptions into behavioural
   intentions besides personal attainments. Studies on the aforementioned
   topic from the view of facilities management are also still flawed plus
   rare. This study aims to explore what are the elements that exist to
   constitute behavioural intentions and personal attainments; which based
   on comprehensive reviews from considerable volume of published journals.
   The results clarified that behavioural intentions consist of favourable
   and unfavourable behavioural intentions; whereas personal attainments
   are theorized about intellectual and self-development gains. (C) 2015
   The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
