Note = {International Conference on Urban Climatology (ICUC 96), ESSEN, GERMANY,
   JUN   10, 1996-JUN 14, 1997},
Abstract = {The paper presents results from a case study of gaseous pollutant
   dispersion in street canyons. Tracer-gas experiments were performed in a
   neutrally stratified wind tunnel. Vehicle emissions were simulated as
   line sources. Concentration profiles along building walls were measured.
   A two-dimensional street canyon was considered as the reference case.
   The influence of systematic parameter variations on the concentration
   field is studied and discussed. Building dimensions, upwind building
   configuration, wind direction and roof geometry were found to be
   important parameters. Data sets from the study may be used for
   evaluation of numerical models and for expert estimates of air quality
   in the urban environment (C) 1999 Elsevier Science Ltd. All rights
   reserved.},
