Pages = {221-226},
Note = {2024 International Conference on Energy and Environment-ICEE-Bringing
   together Engineering and Economics, Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, JUN 06-07, 2024},
Abstract = {Controversy over shale gas development utilizing fracking has been on
   the rise in recent years. The literature focused on the impact of the
   shale gas exploration development provides a general, theoretical, and
   practical perspective on the experience of such activity in different
   countries. Specifically, when it came to Brazil, the literature was
   based on international experience, since this activity is not yet fully
   operational in the country. This research aimed to critically analyse
   the expected positive and negative impacts of shale gas exploration in
   Brazil. For this, we firstly reviewed the international literature and
   then conducted interviews with the potential experts like authors of
   studies and projects, public prosecutors involved, recommended by the
   interviewees, and representatives of the oil and gas sector and
   non-governmental organizations. This approach aimed to collect
   information from the experts' experiences and perceptions that would
   allow to compare, contrast, and complement the findings of the
   literature review to establish a link between the literature and
   Brazil's national reality. The results of the research highlighted the
   great concern about the environmental dimension regarding water
   resources: control of chemicals in the fracking fluid, propagation of
   seismic tremors and possible aquifers `contamination.},
