   Taiwan Univ; Natl Chin Yi Univ Technol; Hotels \& Tourism Ind Assoc;
   Tourism Chamber Commerce; Lingnan Int Grp; Chime Long Grp; Hengda Hotel
   Management Grp; Amer Scholar Press; Jinan Univ, Alumni Assoc},
Abstract = {The concept of native-land planning draws references from Lao Tzu and
   Chuang Tzu's idea of ``nurturing through inaction{''}. With
   ``inaction{''} as the highest level, the concept emphasizes respect for
   nature so as to achieve authenticity of people's life and production in
   the planning process. Concerning the idea and method, native-land
   planning focuses on people being in harmony with nature, advocates
   nature-based as well as residents' oriented ideas, and promotes
   preservation of original life style to offer people the true qualities
   of natural experience and life experience. When applying the idea of
   native-land planning to rural planning, it means refusal of rural areas'
   urbanization and also means prevention of ``urban problems{''} from
   spreading to rural areas in order to preserve rural landscape and
   images.},
