Note = {12th International Conference on Innovation in Urban and Regional
   Planning (INPUT), Univ LAquila, ITALY, SEP 06-08, 2023},
Abstract = {Recently, the concept of a Positive Energy District (PED) has been
   deeply discussed, and Structural Equation Modeling (SEM) has been widely
   used in sustainability studies to model the relationships between latent
   and manifest variables of this concept. This article is presented
   through an educational and fundamental approach to balancing positive
   energies by introducing a basic framework. The latter includes energy
   efficiency functions, energy production functions, and household energy
   consumption. In this article, while describing how to use SEM, the
   authors propose a model including dependent, independent, mediating, and
   moderating variables. The results of data analysis show that the
   introduced model is able to estimate the effect of positive energy
   balance on climate-friendly neighborhoods and environmental
   sustainability indicators. The relationship between energy balance works
   positively and will be a key solution for energy systems that are
   transitioning towards carbon-free urban designs.},
